只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Antigravity route for DeepSeek Harness: local Antigravity CLI (agy) as an LLM provider","id":"gh:1369555128","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-llm-antigravity","slug":"zhangzhangco/dsh-llm-antigravity","topics":["agy","antigravity","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","gemini","llm"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Antigravity route for DeepSeek Harness: local Antigravity CLI (agy) as an LLM provider"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-llm-antigravity"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"An **Antigravity route** for DeepSeek Harness: it registers one LLM provider\n(`antigravity-local` by"},{"id":"p3s2","text":" default) whose requests go to the Antigravity CLI\n(`agy`) installed and signed in on this machine."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"This plugin is not part of the published `@deepseek-ai/*` distribution. It lives\nin the `web` profil"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"e and is mounted through that profile's patch layer, so the\nDSH installation itself is untouched. It"},{"id":"p4s3","text":" is the sibling of\n`dsh-llm-codex` and follows the\nsame shape: one `LlmAdapter`, one route, shipped "},{"id":"p4s4","text":"with its own bundle patch."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Quick start — one command, no patch file to edit:"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"The package declares `dsh.bundle.patch`, so `dsh plugin` appends it to the\nprofile's `dsh.profile.bu"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"ndles` and its `cordis.patch.yml` mounts the\n`llm-antigravity` row on its own. Restart the profile a"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"nd the route appears in\nthe model selector. Other install forms (tarball, linked folder) are in\nShar"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"ing with another machine."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"> This package is intentionally **not published to npm** and keeps\n> `private: true`. The name `dsh-"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"llm-antigravity` on npm belongs to an unrelated\n> implementation by another author; the field is a g"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"uard against publishing over\n> it. GitHub is the distribution channel — see\n> Why GitHub and not npm"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"ard against publishing over\n> it. GitHub is the distribution channel — see\n> Why GitHub and not npm."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"A fresh install runs with the schema defaults, which means **text-only**\n(`textOnly: true`) and **ap"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"proval on** (`skipPermissions: false`). Flipping\neither one is a per-machine decision made in your o"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"wn patch file, not in this\npackage — see Configuration."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## What it is (and is not)"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"`agy` is a **complete agent** with its own tools, terminal sandbox, and approval\nflow. This adapter "},{"id":"p11s2","text":"therefore exposes it as a **text-generation route**:"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"- It forwards the conversation (system prompt, history, tool calls and tool\nresults rendered as text"},{"id":"p12s2","text":") and returns the model's answer.\n- Antigravity's own tool use is **not** reported as harness tool c"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"alls, and DSH\ntool calls are **not** executed by Antigravity. A DSH session on this route\nkeeps its "},{"id":"p12s4","text":"own tools; Antigravity answers from the text it was given.\n- Because Antigravity *has* tools, it wil"},{"id":"p12s5","text":"l try to use them on task-shaped\nprompts. See Tool handling,\nwhich is the single most important thin"},{"id":"p12s6","text":"g to understand about this route."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Choose the MCP path instead if you want DSH tools driven by Antigravity, or\nAntigravity's tools expo"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"th instead if you want DSH tools driven by Antigravity, or\nAntigravity's tools exposed as DSH tools."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## Tool handling: why `textOnly` matters (default on)"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"This is the failure that shaped the plugin, so it is worth stating plainly."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"`agy` decides on its own whether a prompt needs a tool. Ask it something\ntask-shaped — *\"check wheth"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"er this directory is writable\"* — and it calls its own\n`run_command`. In print mode there is nobody "},{"id":"p16s3","text":"to answer the approval prompt, so\nthe call is **auto-denied**, the agent stops, and the turn ends wi"},{"id":"p16s4","text":"th an empty\nresponse. The CLI reports this honestly (`denied_actions:\n[{\"action\":\"command\",\"display_"},{"id":"p16s5","text":"name\":\"RunCommand\"}]`), but the harness only sees\na model that produced no text."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"With `textOnly: true` (the default) the adapter provisions a small custom agent\nand selects it with "},{"id":"p17s2","text":"Only: true` (the default) the adapter provisions a small custom agent\nand selects it with `--agent`:"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"That agent is instructed to answer from the conversation alone and never to\nreach for tools, which t"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"urns the route into what the harness expects. The file\nis created only when it is missing, so an age"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"nt you wrote yourself is never\noverwritten; set `geminiConfigDir` to relocate it, or `provisionAgent"},{"id":"p19s4","text":": false` to\nmanage the file yourself."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"If Antigravity still ends a turn on a denied tool call, the adapter raises an\nactionable error namin"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"g the tool and the two fixes instead of a bare\n\"no assistant message\":"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Set `textOnly: false` plus `skipPermissions: true` only when you actually want\nAntigravity to act on"},{"id":"p22s2","text":" the machine — and accept that its tools then run outside\nthe harness sandbox, with no DSH approval "},{"id":"p22s3","text":"d accept that its tools then run outside\nthe harness sandbox, with no DSH approval in front of them."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"### What tool mode actually does"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Measured on a real run with `textOnly: false` and `skipPermissions: true`:"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"- `agy`'s `init` event reports **57 tools** and `permission_mode:\nalways-proceed`, so nothing is den"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"ied and no `denied_actions` come back;\n- `run_command` executes **in the configured `cwd`** (or the "},{"id":"p25s3","text":"session workspace\nwhen `cwd` is empty) — `pwd` returns that directory;\n- file-producing tools may in"},{"id":"p25s4","text":"stead write into Antigravity's own scratch area,\n`~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/scratch/`, so an artifac"},{"id":"p25s5","text":"t the model reports as\n\"created\" can land outside the workspace you expected. Use `addDirs`\n(`agy --"},{"id":"p25s6","text":"add-dir`) to bring another root into the session workspace, and check\nthe reported path rather than "},{"id":"p25s7","text":"assuming `cwd`;\n- the harness still receives **text only**: Antigravity's tool traffic never\nbecomes"},{"id":"p25s8","text":" DSH tool calls, so nothing appears in the DSH transcript as a tool\ninvocation and no DSH tool execu"},{"id":"p25s9","text":" tool calls, so nothing appears in the DSH transcript as a tool\ninvocation and no DSH tool executes."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"Because the last point surprises people, the two tool layers are worth keeping\napart: `textOnly` con"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"trols **Antigravity's** tools, while the harness's own tools\n(bash, read, write, web) are never in p"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"lay on this route whether `textOnly` is on\nor off."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## Why GitHub and not npm"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"There is no official DSH plugin registry: a plugin is an ordinary package, and\ndiscovery happens thr"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"ough the GitHub `dsh-plugin` topic. This repository is\ndistributed that way, and `private: true` sta"},{"id":"p28s3","text":"ys set for one concrete reason —\nthe name `dsh-llm-antigravity` on npm is already taken by an unrela"},{"id":"p28s4","text":"ted\nimplementation (`zsp1987/dsh-llm-antigravity`). Publishing under the same name\nwould either fail"},{"id":"p28s5","text":" or collide with a package users already have. Install from the\ngit repository instead; the `dsh-plu"},{"id":"p28s6","text":"gin` topic is what makes it discoverable."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"### What does not transfer"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"- **The credential.** Antigravity's sign-in is per machine — run `agy` there if\nit is not signed in "},{"id":"p30s2","text":"yet.\n- **`~/.gemini/config/agents/dsh-text/agent.md`.** The plugin recreates it on\nfirst load, as lo"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"ng as `provisionAgent` is left on.\n- **The catalog cache.** It is refilled by the first `agy models`"},{"id":"p30s4","text":"`provisionAgent` is left on.\n- **The catalog cache.** It is refilled by the first `agy models` call."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
